r)**: Using the Rocket on a triplet of Jacks is overkill ("using a cannon to kill a mosquito"). The Rocket is best saved for winning the game, interrupting a long run, or beating a 2-bomb/quad. It is too early to spend it here when I have a natural counter (AAA).\n3.  **Triple with Pair (Aces with 9s)**: This is the optimal move. It beats the opponent\'s JJJ77 with AAA99. It efficiently utilizes the pair of 9s, which is otherwise a weak hand that would be hard to play. It keeps the powerful pair of 2s and the Rocket in reserve to regain control later for playing out the remaining singles (4, 5, 6, 8, Q, K).\n\nReason:\nThe Triple with Pair (AAA99) allows you to take control of the game while simultaneously offloading 5 cards. Crucially, it gets rid of the weak pair of 9s. By saving the pair of 2s and the Rocket, you maintain 3-4 rounds of guaranteed control (High Card entries), which is sufficient to cover your remaining singles (4, 5, 6, 8, Q, K). Passing would leave you with a clunky hand, and using the Rocket is a waste of resources.\n\nAnswer:\n{"cards": ["♠9", "♣9", "♥A", "♣A", "♦A"]}'}
