he Queen. It\'s the most efficient way to get rid of a card while forcing the opponents to use up their high cards, while also not breaking any structure. I can use the Rocket and 2 to take control later.\n\n**Conclusion:** Play the ♥Q. I must get rid of my trash singles as they are currently a disadvantage. This also helps to clear the road for my Rocket.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: You have a hand with several unconnected singles (5, 6, 8, Q, K) but possess extremely strong control cards: a pair of 2s and the Rocket (Black Joker + Red Joker). The current card on the table is a ♠10, which is a mid-range single. To win, you must actively clear your singles. Passing would allow the opponents (especially the one with 16 cards) to potentially dictate the game type (e.g., switching to pairs or sequences which you are weak against).\n\nReason: The ♥Q is the most efficient play here. It is your lowest single that beats the ♠10. By playing the Queen, you force the opponents to play their high cards (Kings, Ace, or 2s) to beat you. Since you hold the top control cards (2s and the Rocket), you can confidently counter their high cards to regain the lead and continue clearing your low singles. Using a 2 now would be wasteful, and passing gives up initiative.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥Q"]}'}
